<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Texcoco</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Texcocan, Texcocans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Texcoco was a major city-state on the eastern shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-texcoco">Lake Texcoco</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valley-of-mexico">Valley of Mexico</a> and one of the three members of the Aztec Triple Alliance. Renowned as a centre of law, poetry and learning, especially under its ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nezahualcoyotl">Nezahualcoyotl</a>, it received two-fifths of the alliance's tribute revenues. Factions of the Texcocans sided with the Spanish during the conquest.</p></div>
